			"notes": "# Create Fabric Optimized 6.0.8.1 + Flywheel alecperf.7\n\nPerformance-focused unofficial build of Create Fabric for Minecraft 1.20.1.\n\n## Versions\n\n- Minecraft: 1.20.1\n- Create Fabric: 6.0.8.1\n- Flywheel: 1.0.6-alecperf.7\n- Java: 17\n- Fabric Loader build environment: 0.17.2\n- Fabric API build environment: 0.92.6+1.20.1\n\n## Optimizations\n\n- Cached packed material values for instanced draw calls.\n- Eliminated temporary array allocations during embedded matrix uniform uploads.\n- Reused native staging memory for changed instance-buffer uploads.\n- Uploads only changed light-section spans during steady-state updates.\n- Reused native staging memory for instanced light LUT uploads.\n- Skips redundant shader-program binds between consecutive compatible draws.\n- Skips redundant material render-state setup between consecutive equivalent materials.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Flywheel Fabric and Create Fabric builds completed successfully.\n- The distributable JAR contains Flywheel 1.0.6-alecperf.7.\n- Focused correctness checks and isolated performance benchmarks passed.\n- In-game validation completed successfully.\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall the attached JAR as the Create mod.\n\nThe optimized Flywheel build is already embedded. Do not install another Flywheel JAR alongside it.\n\nBack up important worlds before changing mod builds.\n\n## Disclaimer\n\nThis is an unofficial optimization fork and is not an official Create or Flywheel release.\n\nPerformance improvements depend on the rendered scene, hardware, graphics driver, installed mods, and selected Flywheel backend."
		}
